    "en":  {
               "headline":  "Record quarter, but AEHR falls 16.9% in a chip sell-off and breaks its lower band",
               "technical":  "The trend is clearly down. AEHR closed at 39.84 USD on 2026-11-20, below all three exponential moving averages (EMAs, smoothed average prices): EMA50 at 68.39, EMA100 at 75.39 and EMA200 at 70.94. The 50-day line has fallen under both longer lines, which shows a strong uptrend that has rolled over. MACD (a trend-momentum gauge) is -6.93, below its signal line at -6.38, with a negative histogram (-0.55), so downside momentum is still building. RSI 14 (a 0–100 momentum gauge where under 30 means oversold) is 32.59, close to oversold but not there yet. Price closed below the lower Bollinger Band (42.51; the bands track normal price swings around the 20-day average of 56.12). That marks an unusually stretched move, and these often see a short bounce, but they can also keep \u0027walking the band\u0027 lower. Volume of 3.87M was about 1.29x the 20-day average, which confirms real selling. The stock is about 73% below its 52-week high of 147.4 and sits in the bottom sixth of its range, above the 18.7 low. The day\u0027s low of 39.3 is the nearest support, and 42.5–45.9 is the first resistance zone.",
               "fundamental":  "The business is going the opposite way to the share price. On 2026-11-02 Aehr reported record Q1 FY2027 revenue of $33.0M, up 200% year on year. Bookings were $46.7M and backlog was $100.9M ($109.3M effective as of Nov 1). Non-GAAP EPS was $0.28. The company raised its FY2027 revenue guidance to $150M, about triple FY2026, with non-GAAP net income of at least 20% of revenue. On AI, its lead hyperscale customer qualified a second AI processor on Sonoma package-level burn-in, and that customer expects a larger ramp in calendar 2027. A major AI accelerator and CPU supplier bought a full FOX-XP wafer-level test cell for evaluation in Taiwan. The weak spots are cash, which fell to $105.1M from $116.5M, inventory, which rose to $53.1M, and continued reliance on a few customers.",
               "news":  [
                            "2026-10-07: Aehr announced about $6M in follow-on Sonoma orders from its lead hyperscale customer for a next-generation AI processor, with production expected to ramp in calendar 2027.",
                            "2026-11-02: Q1 FY2027 revenue hit a record $33.0M (+200% YoY), backlog reached $100.9M, and FY2027 guidance was raised to $150M. Consensus comparisons differ by source: one says revenue beat, another says it missed a ~$37.7M estimate.",
                            "Around 2026-11-05: the stock fell about 17% from $60.84 after Jefferies cut its target from $175 to $140 and Lake Street from $110 to $90. Both kept Buy ratings.",
                            "2026-11-20: shares fell 16.9% to 39.84 with no company-specific news. The move was part of a broad semiconductor sell-off that also hit Micron, AMD and Onto Innovation. AEHR\u0027s beta is roughly 3.4, meaning it typically moves about three times as much as the market."
                        ],
               "caution":  "AEHR is a very high-beta stock (beta about 3.4) and has lost about 73% from its 52-week high, even as fundamentals improved. That tells you sentiment and sector flows, not quarterly results, are setting the price right now. A large share of revenue still depends on one hyperscaler and one wafer-level AI customer, and customer forecasts are non-binding. The FOX-XP production decision from the new AI processor supplier is not expected until several months after installation in early 2027. Any delay or loss there would hit expectations hard. Inventory growth and cash burn also need watching.",
               "opportunity":  "The company is delivering: revenue tripled year on year, guidance went up, and there is a $100M+ backlog to support it. The stock trades at 39.84 USD on 2026-11-20, near the low end of its range, while RSI is close to oversold and price sits below the lower Bollinger Band. If the semiconductor sell-off eases, a stretched move like this can mean-revert toward the 20-day average of 56.12. Longer term, the potential FOX-XP win and the hyperscaler\u0027s second AI processor ramp in 2027 could widen the customer base beyond the current concentration.",
               "risks":  [
                             "Customer concentration: one hyperscaler and one wafer-level AI customer drive most of the AI revenue.",
                             "The FOX-XP evaluation may not convert into a high-volume production order.",
                             "Extreme volatility (beta about 3.4) and sector-wide semiconductor sell-offs.",
                             "Inventory rose to $53.1M and cash fell to $105.1M, so execution risk is rising.",
                             "Silicon-carbide demand remains weak, and the company has exposure to Taiwan and geopolitics."
                         ],
               "summary":  "AEHR\u0027s chart is bearish. Price is below all three EMAs, MACD is negative, and the stock closed below the lower Bollinger Band on above-average volume after a 16.9% drop on 2026-11-20. The news does not explain the selling: the 2026-11-02 quarter set a record and guidance went up. The decline reflects analyst target cuts and a sector-wide chip sell-off on a high-beta stock. The niche-burn-in moat thesis is intact, and its AI customer pipeline is widening. The key test is whether the FOX-XP evaluation turns into production orders in 2027."
